he nuts and bolts might  mean studying some grammar it might mean  reviewing your flashcards in my own case  at Linc I like to go into words that  I've saved and edit out the save phrase  tag them invest some time in these words  that I've saved even if I don't do it  for all of them if I do it for some of  them for example in the case of check to  try and get a handle on the cases you  know there's always this sort of  incidental learning factor if I do it  for a hundred nouns then I will start to  see it happening in another few hundred  dollars so I don't have to do it for all  hundred or a thousand or five thousand  dollars that I've that I'd say but the  question is timing when is it worth my  while to invest time in these nuts and  bolts whether it be grammar review  whether it be refining these words and  phrases that I've saved in link whether  it be vocabulary review when is the  right time to do it I happen to believe  that that one shouldn't do the same  thing every day that you know I gonna  spend yeah again if you have eight hours  a day to spend that doesn't matter but  if you have an hour or two to spend you  have to try to maximize the benefit of  your activity so if I'm tired I'm gonna  just listen or read it's easy to do I  might even throw on a video and even in  so far as going after the nuts and bolts  now in check I'm much more motivated to  do that now than I was at the beginning  at the beginning I had no words  it was just noise to me was just so many  words on a sheet of paper when I tried  to read it I have now accumulated enough  words that I can kind of pick my way  through a lot of these text  I'm ringing in from from the newspaper  but I'm a little confused as to the  cases and which prepositions take which  cases and these endings because in Czech  you know depending on their soft eye you  know the dictionary gives me all kinds  of stuff about soft vowels and or at  least soft I can't remember what it was  but they're soft and hard in there but  the main point is that there's no  regular pattern you know in terms of  which ending is identified with which  case I or you like II or whatever could  be the genitive singular genitive plural  dative singular plural it's all over the  map so yeah I've kind of looked over the  tables but now what I'm doing is I'm  going through the texts that I've  studied and either in the vocab section  or even on the lesson page I'm opening  up all these words that have the saved  phrase with them tidying up the phrase  and identifying and I've got open on my  computer a handy web page which has all  the check noun cases on them so I made  sure that I got it right a target right  and I do this and I feel that I'm really  getting a handle on it now that the  timing is right for me now to be doing  this activity you know if I were at some  course it would be the teacher who  decides when they're going to teach the  genitive like I you know or the data  ever or whatever and I might not I might  not be receptive to it so I think the  timing is so key in language learning in  terms of what activity we choose to do  in terms of what we want to do at a  given time either retired in terms of  what we're interested in also in terms  of of when our brain is most likely to  retain this information or to to to make  some use of it I mean the purpose of  studying the nuts and bolts whether it  be reading some grammar rule reviewing  some tables again as I was just saying  tagging some  words and phrases for their cases and  you know doing your Anki flashcards the  reason you do this is because in my  opinion it makes you more attentive when  you're listening and reading so that  you're when you're listening and reading  you're really able to to absorb to mine  those texts for all the structural  patterns that are there so that they can  become part of you so to summarize then  I think timing is very important timing  to match what you want to do timing to  match when a particular activity is  likely to me be the most effective and  very often that'll be when you feel like  doing it and so because I'm sure we have  all had the experience that you will  study a table of declensions or  conjugations and I mean all you're doing  is looking at it really it's not  penetrating its you can review it today  you can review it tomorrow the next day  nothing is happening because it's not  the right time the the soil is not  absorbing the nutrients you know that  you're trying to bring in it's the wrong  time whereas if it's the right time if  you want it you've noticed you've  struggled you want you want some answers  now for these you know language  phenomena that your brain has been  exposed to and is struggling to sort you  know to create some patterns for and now  these this review of the nuts and bolts  really helps you so I think I was asked  once where I spend my time and of course  I spent most of my time listening for  the main for the reason that it is so  easy to do I I in my car whatever I can  always listen I like to read as well so  reading and linking is a lot of my time  the nuts and bolts part of it is a much  smaller portion but I think it's very  very beneficial to go go at it when  you're in the mood when you have the  patience to do it to go at it in a  concentrated manner and if you really  want to do it then at that time you're  probably going to be more successful  doing it so there you have it that's you  know I I just wanted to say that I think  the time  timing of which of these output at least  activities input-output nuts-and-bolts  which one you do win is very important  and it's very important that the learner  be in charge of that process because if  the teacher is gonna force you to do  something that you don't want to do then  again you're not gonna get the benefit  and so while I am very much as you know  from my video is an input oriented  learner and I feel that input is key  that the input equals understanding your  understanding always has to be up here  your output ability is gonna be lower  than graslie increase but if you haven't  got this strong input base this strong  comprehension you're gonna struggle I  always struggle with your output but  there's also the nuts and bolts so  you've got to find the time which suits  you  to do these and and if you hit the  timing right your learning will become  much much more efficient so there you go  I look forward to your comments thank  you for listening
 

